<title>PORTUGAL: Ships wait outside Lisbon port due pilots' strike.</title>
<headline>Ships wait outside Lisbon port due pilots' strike.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>At least three ships were prevented from entering Lisbon port because of an indefinite pilots' strike that began at 0600 GMT, officials said.</p>
<p>The pilots met at a dock in Lisbon to discuss what action to take after nine pilots were detained last week on corruption charges.</p>
<p>A source in the Portuguese Association of Navigation Agents said if the strike persisted, the government may have to authorise ships that regularly travel to and from Lisbon port to do so without the aid of a pilot under their own responsibility.</p>
<p>Portuguese pilots demanding better working conditions previously went on strike in September 1991. --Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
